module

public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.HilbertFunction

/-!
# A quadric in `ℙ²` is cut out by its quadratic form

Section 54.12 of the source identifies the exceptional curve `E` of the blowup of a rational
double point in its closed point with the zero scheme of a quadratic form inside
`ℙ²_κ = Proj(κ[t₁, t₂, t₃])`. The graded ring behind that identification is
`⨁ₙ 𝔪ⁿ/𝔪ⁿ⁺¹`, a quotient of `κ[t₁, t₂, t₃]` because `𝔪` needs three generators, and the only
input the source uses to pin the quotient down is the dimension count
`dim_κ(𝔪ⁿ/𝔪ⁿ⁺¹) = 2n + 1`.

This file supplies the step which turns that count into a statement about the homogeneous ideal:
a homogeneous ideal `I ⊆ κ[t₁, t₂, t₃]` which contains a nonzero quadratic form `q` and whose
quotient has Hilbert function at least `2n + 1` in every degree is the principal ideal `(q)`.
Nothing more is needed, because `κ[t₁, t₂, t₃]/(q)` has Hilbert function exactly `2n + 1`: the
degree-`n` part of `κ[t₁, t₂, t₃]` has dimension `binom(n + 2, n) = binom(n, 2) + 2n + 1`, and
multiplication by `q` injects the degree-`(n − 2)` part into the degree-`n` part of `(q)`, so the
`binom(n, 2)` dimensions of the ideal are already accounted for by multiples of `q` and there is
no room for any further relation.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.finrank_gradedPieceS_three`: `dim_κ(κ[t₁, t₂, t₃]_n) = binom(n, 2) + 2n + 1`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.finrank_gradedPieceS_le_finrank_gradedPieceI_of_mem`: multiplication by a
  nonzero homogeneous element of degree `e` of an ideal `I` injects the degree-`m` part of the
  polynomial ring into the degree-`(m + e)` part of `I`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.eq_span_singleton_of_hilbertFunction_two_mul_add_one`: **a homogeneous ideal
  of `κ[t₁, t₂, t₃]` containing a nonzero quadratic form `q`, whose quotient has Hilbert function
  at least `2n + 1` in every degree, is `(q)`.** This is the arithmetic content of
  `E = V(q) ⊂ ℙ²_κ`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isHomogeneous_eq_span_singleton_of_hilbertFunction`: the same with
  the quadratic form produced rather than given — a homogeneous ideal of `κ[t₁, t₂, t₃]` whose
  quotient has Hilbert function exactly `2n + 1` is generated by one nonzero quadratic form.

## Implementation notes

The graded pieces are those of `StacksFrontier/RingTheory/HilbertFunction.lean`:
`Stacks.HilbertFunction.PolynomialQuotient.gradedPieceS k d n` is the degree-`n` part of
`k[X₁, …, X_d]`, `gradedPieceI I n` is the degree-`n` part of an ideal, and `hilbertFunction I n`
is `dim_k(S_n) − dim_k(I_n)` with truncated subtraction, which is honest because `I_n ⊆ S_n`.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached. The statement is a step in the unnumbered discussion of
Section 54.12, whose three numbered items (Tags 0BGC, 0BGD, 0BGE) are registered elsewhere, and
it is only one half of the identification: what remains is the graded surjection
`κ[t₁, t₂, t₃] → ⨁ₙ 𝔪ⁿ/𝔪ⁿ⁺¹` and the identification of `E` with the `Proj` of its target.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BGE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BGE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00K3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00K3)
-/

@[expose] public section

open Stacks.HilbertFunction.PolynomialQuotient

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

variable {k : Type*} [Field k]

/-! ### Finite dimensionality of the graded pieces -/

/-- The degree-`n` part of `k[X₁, …, X_d]` is a finite-dimensional `k`-vector space: it is
spanned by the finitely many monomials of total degree `n`. -/
public theorem finiteDimensional_gradedPieceS (k : Type*) [Field k] (d n : ℕ) :
    FiniteDimensional k (gradedPieceS k d n) :=
  (Submodule.fg_iff_finiteDimensional _).mp (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule_fg (Fin d) k n)

/-- The degree-`n` part of an ideal of `k[X₁, …, X_d]` is a finite-dimensional `k`-vector space,
being contained in the degree-`n` part of the polynomial ring. -/
public theorem finiteDimensional_gradedPieceI {d : ℕ} (I : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin d) k))
    (n : ℕ) : FiniteDimensional k (gradedPieceI I n) := by
  have := finiteDimensional_gradedPieceS k d n
  exact Submodule.finiteDimensional_inf_right (I.restrictScalars k) (gradedPieceS k d n)

/-! ### The dimensions of the graded pieces in three variables -/

/-- `binom(n + 2, n) = binom(n, 2) + 2n + 1`, the dimension count behind the Hilbert function of
a quadric surface: the degree-`n` part of a polynomial ring in three variables has dimension
`binom(n + 2, n)`, and `binom(n, 2)` of those dimensions are multiples of a fixed quadratic
form. -/
public theorem choose_add_two_self (n : ℕ) : (n + 2).choose n = n.choose 2 + (2 * n + 1) := by
  induction n with
  | zero => decide
  | succ n ih =>
      have h1 : (n + 1 + 2).choose (n + 1) = (n + 2).choose n + (n + 2).choose (n + 1) :=
        Nat.choose_succ_succ (n + 2) n
      have h2 : (n + 2).choose (n + 1) = n + 2 := Nat.choose_succ_self_right (n + 1)
      have h4 : (n + 1).choose 2 = n.choose 1 + n.choose 2 := Nat.choose_succ_succ n 1
      rw [Nat.choose_one_right] at h4
      omega

/-- **The dimensions of the graded pieces of `k[t₁, t₂, t₃]`:**
`dim_k(k[t₁, t₂, t₃]_n) = binom(n, 2) + 2n + 1`. -/
public theorem finrank_gradedPieceS_three (k : Type*) [Field k] (n : ℕ) :
    Module.finrank k (gradedPieceS k 3 n) = n.choose 2 + (2 * n + 1) := by
  rw [finrank_gradedPieceS, show n + 3 - 1 = n + 2 from rfl]
  exact choose_add_two_self n

/-! ### Multiplication by a homogeneous element of the ideal -/

/-- A polynomial lies in the degree-`n` part of an ideal iff it is in the ideal and homogeneous
of degree `n`. -/
private theorem mem_gradedPieceI_iff {d : ℕ} {I : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin d) k)}
    {p : MvPolynomial (Fin d) k} {n : ℕ} : p ∈ gradedPieceI I n ↔ p ∈ I ∧ p.IsHomogeneous n :=
  Submodule.mem_inf.trans (and_congr_right fun _ => MvPolynomial.mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _)

/-- **Multiplication by a nonzero homogeneous element of degree `e` of an ideal `I` injects the
degree-`m` part of `k[X₁, …, X_d]` into the degree-`(m + e)` part of `I`.** The product lies in
`I` because one factor does, it is homogeneous of degree `m + e` because both factors are
homogeneous, and the map is injective because the polynomial ring over a field is a domain. -/
public theorem finrank_gradedPieceS_le_finrank_gradedPieceI_of_mem {d : ℕ}
    {q : MvPolynomial (Fin d) k} {e : ℕ} (hq : q.IsHomogeneous e) (hq0 : q ≠ 0)
    {I : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin d) k)} (hqI : q ∈ I) (m : ℕ) :
    Module.finrank k (gradedPieceS k d m) ≤ Module.finrank k (gradedPieceI I (m + e)) := by
  have := finiteDimensional_gradedPieceI I (m + e)
  have hmem : ∀ p ∈ gradedPieceS k d m, q * p ∈ gradedPieceI I (m + e) := fun p hp =>
    mem_gradedPieceI_iff.mpr ⟨I.mul_mem_right p hqI,
      add_comm e m ▸ hq.mul ((MvPolynomial.mem_homogeneousSubmodule _ _).mp hp)⟩
  let F : gradedPieceS k d m →ₗ[k] gradedPieceI I (m + e) :=
    { toFun := fun p => ⟨q * (p : MvPolynomial (Fin d) k), hmem p p.2⟩
      map_add' := fun a b => Subtype.ext (by simp [mul_add])
      map_smul' := fun c a => Subtype.ext (by simp [mul_smul_comm]) }
  exact F.finrank_le_finrank_of_injective fun a b hab =>
    Subtype.ext (mul_left_cancel₀ hq0 (congrArg Subtype.val hab))

/-! ### The homogeneous ideal of a quadric -/

/-- **A homogeneous ideal of `k[t₁, t₂, t₃]` which contains a nonzero quadratic form `q` and
whose quotient has Hilbert function at least `2n + 1` in every degree is the principal ideal
`(q)`.**

This is the arithmetic content of the identification `E = V(q) ⊂ ℙ²_κ` in Section 54.12 of the
source: the homogeneous coordinate ring of `E` is `⨁ₙ 𝔪ⁿ/𝔪ⁿ⁺¹`, a quotient of `κ[t₁, t₂, t₃]`
with Hilbert function `2n + 1`, and the relation of degree two the source exhibits already
generates all of the relations.

The proof is a dimension count in each degree. The degree-`n` part of `k[t₁, t₂, t₃]` has
dimension `binom(n, 2) + 2n + 1`, so the hypothesis bounds the degree-`n` part of `I` above by
`binom(n, 2)`; multiplication by `q` bounds the degree-`n` part of `(q)` below by the same
`binom(n, 2)`; and `(q) ⊆ I`. The two graded pieces therefore coincide in every degree, and a
homogeneous ideal is determined by its graded pieces. -/
public theorem eq_span_singleton_of_hilbertFunction_two_mul_add_one
    {q : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k} (hq : q.IsHomogeneous 2) (hq0 : q ≠ 0)
    {I : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k)}
    (hIhom : Ideal.IsHomogeneous (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin 3) k) I)
    (hqI : q ∈ I) (hhilb : ∀ n, 2 * n + 1 ≤ hilbertFunction I n) :
    I = Ideal.span {q} := by
  have hub : ∀ n, Module.finrank k (gradedPieceI I n) ≤ n.choose 2 := by
    intro n
    have h1 := hhilb n
    unfold hilbertFunction at h1
    rw [finrank_gradedPieceS_three] at h1
    omega
  have hlb : ∀ n, n.choose 2 ≤ Module.finrank k (gradedPieceI (Ideal.span {q}) n) := by
    intro n
    rcases lt_or_ge n 2 with hn | hn
    · rw [Nat.choose_eq_zero_of_lt hn]
      exact Nat.zero_le _
    · have h := finrank_gradedPieceS_le_finrank_gradedPieceI_of_mem hq hq0
        (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self q) (n - 2)
      rwa [Nat.sub_add_cancel hn, finrank_gradedPieceS,
        show n - 2 + 3 - 1 = n - 2 + 2 from rfl, Nat.sub_add_cancel hn, Nat.choose_symm hn] at h
  have hspanle : Ideal.span {q} ≤ I := (Ideal.span_le).mpr (by simpa using hqI)
  have hpiece : ∀ n, gradedPieceI I n = gradedPieceI (Ideal.span {q}) n := by
    intro n
    have := finiteDimensional_gradedPieceI I n
    refine (Submodule.eq_of_le_of_finrank_le ?_ ((hub n).trans (hlb n))).symm
    intro x hx
    obtain ⟨hx1, hx2⟩ := mem_gradedPieceI_iff.mp hx
    exact mem_gradedPieceI_iff.mpr ⟨hspanle hx1, hx2⟩
  refine le_antisymm (fun y hy => ?_) hspanle
  have hcomp : ∀ i, MvPolynomial.homogeneousComponent i y ∈ Ideal.span {q} := by
    intro i
    have h1 : MvPolynomial.homogeneousComponent i y ∈ gradedPieceI I i :=
      mem_gradedPieceI_iff.mpr ⟨MvPolynomial.homogeneousComponent_mem_of_mem hIhom hy i,
        MvPolynomial.homogeneousComponent_isHomogeneous i y⟩
    rw [hpiece i] at h1
    exact (mem_gradedPieceI_iff.mp h1).1
  have hsum : (∑ i ∈ Finset.range (y.totalDegree + 1), MvPolynomial.homogeneousComponent i y)
      ∈ Ideal.span {q} := Submodule.sum_mem _ fun i _ => hcomp i
  rwa [MvPolynomial.sum_homogeneousComponent] at hsum

/-- **A homogeneous ideal of `k[t₁, t₂, t₃]` whose quotient has Hilbert function `2n + 1` is
generated by a single nonzero quadratic form.**

The quadratic form is not an input: the degree-two part of `k[t₁, t₂, t₃]` has dimension `6`,
which exceeds the prescribed `dim_k(k[t₁, t₂, t₃]/I)₂ = 5` by exactly one, so the degree-two part
of `I` is a line and any nonzero element of it is the quadratic form. This is the shape in which
Section 54.12 of the source produces `q`: three generators of `𝔪` have six products `xₚxᵩ` with
`p ≤ q`, one more than `dim_κ(𝔪²/𝔪³) = 5`, so there is exactly one relation among them modulo
`𝔪³`.

Together with
`AlgebraicGeometry.eq_span_singleton_of_hilbertFunction_two_mul_add_one` this says that the
homogeneous coordinate ring of a scheme with the Hilbert function of a plane conic is
`k[t₁, t₂, t₃]/(q)` on the nose. -/
public theorem exists_isHomogeneous_eq_span_singleton_of_hilbertFunction
    {I : Ideal (MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k)}
    (hIhom : Ideal.IsHomogeneous (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin 3) k) I)
    (hhilb : ∀ n, hilbertFunction I n = 2 * n + 1) :
    ∃ q : MvPolynomial (Fin 3) k, q.IsHomogeneous 2 ∧ q ≠ 0 ∧ I = Ideal.span {q} := by
  have := finiteDimensional_gradedPieceS k 3 2
  have h6 : Module.finrank k (gradedPieceS k 3 2) = 6 := by
    rw [finrank_gradedPieceS_three]
    decide
  have hle : Module.finrank k (gradedPieceI I 2) ≤ Module.finrank k (gradedPieceS k 3 2) :=
    Submodule.finrank_mono (show gradedPieceI I 2 ≤ gradedPieceS k 3 2 from inf_le_right)
  have h2 := hhilb 2
  unfold hilbertFunction at h2
  rw [h6] at h2 hle
  have hd : Module.finrank k (gradedPieceI I 2) = 1 := by omega
  have hne : gradedPieceI I 2 ≠ ⊥ := by
    intro h
    rw [h] at hd
    simp at hd
  obtain ⟨q, hqmem, hq0⟩ := Submodule.ne_bot_iff _ |>.mp hne
  obtain ⟨hqI, hqhom⟩ := mem_gradedPieceI_iff.mp hqmem
  exact ⟨q, hqhom, hq0, eq_span_singleton_of_hilbertFunction_two_mul_add_one hqhom hq0 hIhom
    hqI fun n => (hhilb n).ge⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
